      "key": "iface_binary",
      "candidate": "EXP_020 binary input code",
      "init": "shadow ~ N(0,1), thr_in = 0",
      "derivation": "dL/dshadow = dL/dB * atan_grad(shadow - thr_in, alpha). The surrogate derivative is strictly positive everywhere and peaks at alpha/2 = 1.0, so the straight-through path is reachable. Predicted separately: the RATIO will be BELOW 1, because a shadow drawn from N(0,1) sits where atan_grad is about 0.09-1.0 rather than at its peak, so the code's gradient is attenuated relative to a dense embedding's. An attenuated gradient is not fatal (Adam is scale-free per parameter); an exactly zero one would be.",
