    {
      "key": "nm_g0",
      "candidate": "EXP_021 local modulator",
      "init": "proposed (exact nesting), kappa = 0",
      "derivation": "dL/dkappa_c = sum_{b,t} (dL/dcur'_{b,t,c}) * cur_{b,t,c} * DA_{b,t}, which is nonzero at kappa = 0 because the factor (1 + kappa*DA) is then 1 and every downstream adjoint is the BASELINE's. But the predictor reaches the loss ONLY through that factor: dL/da = (dL/dDA)*(dDA/dphi)*(dphi/da) and dL/dDA is proportional to kappa. At kappa = 0 all three of nm_a, nm_b and nm_log_tau are EXACTLY zero, by the same backward-induction argument that makes #1's w = 0 a saddle. This is EXP_004 2.2's pattern and it takes EXP_004's remedy: a pre-registered nonzero fallback.",
